# function big(u) { ..; u.k = "s" }  const o = { k: 1 };  big(launder(o));  print(o.k + 1)
# big gives up at the work limit. Its parameter is the unknown value, which at run time is o. The last run of its statements sees every member of every operand again,
# the unknown object among them, so the store reaches the location of the unknown object that o aliases: o.k is not the number alone.
# An object that has not escaped keeps what it holds under the same name.
# OPTIONS: limit=MaxFlowWorkPerFunction:64
# LOSS: MaxFlowWorkPerFunction f1
# RUN: flow-solve nodes
# CHECK-NOT: DeclaredPart(L0#{{*}}, 0) = {1}
# CHECK: DeclaredPart(L1#{{*}}, 0) = {1}

